nodes.body:
@mickqian Thanks for clarifying the decision on this pack-kernel-only PR. I agree that its ~1% pack improvement, with no measurable full-block gain, is not enough to justify this additional fast path.

Could you please take another look at the separate, related zero-copy receive PR #37521 and reopen that one for review? Its earlier four-phase H200 Wan2.2-TI2V-5B A/B reported a 4.00%–7.22% improvement in the complete input-A2A → FlashAttention → output-A2A block and a 1.83%–2.02% improvement in the five-step denoising stage. The request wall-time results were 0.16% and 2.32% at the two resolutions. Those measurements are for #37521, not for the pack-kernel change in this PR.

I have now rebased the #37521 source branch onto `main` at `23a1f53fc` (branch head `27be4d12b`). On H200, its 10 focused CUDA tests pass, and the actual NCCL path produces bit-exact results on 4 and 8 GPUs for FP16 and BF16. The fresh 4/8-GPU timings cover only the input exchange, not a new end-to-end model run; the model-level figures above are from the earlier A/B in #37521. The rebased source branch is ready if you are willing to reopen #37521. Thanks!

